        "title": "Channels and Distribution",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This is the **Place** P: getting the offering to the buyer, when and where they\nwant it. A **marketing channel** (distribution channel) is the set of\ninterdependent organizations that move a product from producer to consumer. The\nlandscape runs from the producer, through intermediaries, to the buyer — across\nboth physical and digital paths."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md#003",
      "path": [
        "06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:marketing:06-channels-and-distribution, git-history:marketing:06-channels-and-distribution]",
        "canonical_path": "marketing/06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md",
        "concepts": "[channel design, distribution, retail, omnichannel, channel conflict, place]",
        "current_path": "marketing/06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:marketing:channels-and-distribution",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "marketing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[distribution channel]",
        "section": "marketing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Channels and Distribution",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                       DISTRIBUTION CHANNEL                              |\n|                                                                         |\n|  PRODUCER                                              CONSUMER         |\n|     |                                                     ^             |\n|     |   DIRECT (0 levels)                                 |             |\n|     o-----------------------------------------------------+             |\n|     |                                                     |             |\n|     |   ONE LEVEL          .----------.                   |             |\n|     o--------------------> | RETAILER | ------------------+             |\n|     |                      '----------'                   |             |\n|     |                                                     |             |\n|     |   TWO LEVELS    .-----------.    .----------.        |            |\n|     o---------------> | WHOLESALER| -> | RETAILER | ------+             |\n|     |                 '-----------'    '----------'        |            |\n|     |                                                     |             |\n|     |   THREE+    .-------.  .-------.  .--------.         |            |\n|     o-----------> | AGENT |->| WHSLR |->| RETLR  | -------+             |\n|                   '-------'  '-------'  '--------'                      |\n|                                                                         |\n|  More levels = more reach, less control + lower margin per unit.        |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md#004",
      "path": [
        "06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:marketing:06-channels-and-distribution, git-history:marketing:06-channels-and-distribution]",
        "canonical_path": "marketing/06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md",
        "concepts": "[channel design, distribution, retail, omnichannel, channel conflict, place]",
        "current_path": "marketing/06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:marketing:channels-and-distribution",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "marketing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[distribution channel]",
        "section": "marketing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Channels and Distribution",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Read left-to-right by levels**: each intermediary you add extends reach but\ncosts margin and control. The bridge: a distribution channel is a **delivery\npipeline with middleware** — each hop adds reach/caching/locality but also\nlatency, cost, and a loss of end-to-end control. Direct-to-consumer is removing\nthe middleware to own the client relationship."
    },
