      "text": "## What Channels Actually Do (Channel Functions)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md#007",
      "path": [
        "06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:marketing:06-channels-and-distribution, git-history:marketing:06-channels-and-distribution]",
        "canonical_path": "marketing/06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md",
        "concepts": "[channel design, distribution, retail, omnichannel, channel conflict, place]",
        "current_path": "marketing/06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:marketing:channels-and-distribution",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "marketing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[distribution channel]",
        "section": "marketing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Channels and Distribution",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Intermediaries are not just markup — they perform functions someone must do.\nRemoving an intermediary does not remove its *work*; it transfers the work to you\nor the customer."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md#008",
      "path": [
        "06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:marketing:06-channels-and-distribution, git-history:marketing:06-channels-and-distribution]",
        "canonical_path": "marketing/06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md",
        "concepts": "[channel design, distribution, retail, omnichannel, channel conflict, place]",
        "current_path": "marketing/06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:marketing:channels-and-distribution",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "marketing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[distribution channel]",
        "section": "marketing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Channels and Distribution",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                  CHANNEL FUNCTIONS                              |\n|                                                                 |\n|  INFORMATION    market intelligence, demand signals             |\n|  PROMOTION      local persuasion, merchandising                 |\n|  CONTACT        finding + reaching buyers                       |\n|  MATCHING       assortment, fitting offer to buyer needs        |\n|  NEGOTIATION    reaching terms, transferring ownership          |\n|  ----------     (the above complete the transaction)            |\n|  PHYSICAL DIST  transport, storage, logistics                   |\n|  FINANCING      credit, carrying inventory                      |\n|  RISK TAKING    bearing the risk of carrying stock              |\n|  ----------     (the above fulfill the transaction)             |\n|                                                                 |\n|  KEY LAW: you can eliminate the intermediary, but NOT the       |\n|  function. The work shifts to producer or customer.             |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md#009",
      "path": [
        "06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:marketing:06-channels-and-distribution, git-history:marketing:06-channels-and-distribution]",
        "canonical_path": "marketing/06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md",
        "concepts": "[channel design, distribution, retail, omnichannel, channel conflict, place]",
        "current_path": "marketing/06-CHANNELS-AND-DISTRIBUTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:marketing:channels-and-distribution",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "marketing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[distribution channel]",
        "section": "marketing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Channels and Distribution",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This is the single most important channel idea. \"Cutting out the middleman\" sounds\nlike pure savings, but the middleman's *functions* (warehousing, last-mile, credit,\nreturns, local presence) still have to be performed and paid for. The bridge: it's\nlike removing a caching/CDN layer — you don't remove the need for fast local\ndelivery, you just have to provide it yourself."
    },
